# The emitted-C# evidence is committed as `*.g.cs.txt`, never `*.g.cs`.
#
# Two reasons, and both matter:
#   1. the Calor-first guard rejects a NEW `.cs` path anywhere in the tree, and
#      these files are transcripts of compiler output, not sources;
#   2. an older copy of `experiments/spike_artifacts.py` wrote `.g.cs`, so a
#      stale checkout can still drop one of these next to the real evidence.
#
# Ignoring the bare form means such a stray can never be committed, and the
# committed `.txt` evidence stays the only thing a reviewer sees.
before/*.g.cs
after/*.g.cs
